Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:43:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zebridge 42: a subject may be longer than 255 bytes

validateSubject applied the 255 of the NAME rules (ADR-6: stream, consumer
and bucket names) to subjects. A subject has no such limit on the wire:
nats-server 2.15.1 delivers a core subject of 3000 bytes and serves
JetStream API subjects of 550 bytes. The new bound is 1024 bytes
(max_subject_len), a quarter of the server's default control line; names
keep 255. NATS_ZIG_NOTES.md: entry 43.

